WEBVTT

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.490
Well, what style should we play?

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.010
Style?

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:24.090
One-on-one fighting game style,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.700
or one-on-many RPG style?

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.750
Ah, I get it.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.440
Sorry, though.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.650
If you want to play video games,
play them at home.

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.260
At the very least,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.600
this is not the place for them.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:21.030
March 26 15:40

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.830
Here, darling. Open wide.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.340
That's really good!

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.760
Really? It's the flavor of love!

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:44.410
Mina, we're on a plane. Sit in your 
seat and fasten your seat belt.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:47.730
My seat belt <i>is</i> fastened.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.620
See?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:56.980
(Always wear your seat belt 
when on an airplane)

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:55.980
Always wear your seat belt 
when on an airplane.

00:02:57.630 --> 00:03:00.600
<i>That's wrong... That is completely wrong!</i>

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:01.990
Blaze!

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:06.820
Why don't you say something 
to her... Not... again...

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.920
Kill you all...

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.960
Kill you... Kill you...

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.230
<i>Is he... talking in his sleep? 
Singing in his sleep?</i>

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.390
<i>You know, I don't even care anymore.</i>

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:31.580
<i>We would like to thank you all 
for choosing Cavalier Airlines.</i>

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:36.190
<i>This is flight 123 bound for Couljours.</i>

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.530
There you go...

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.450
I'll let you eat your fill soon.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.210
So long as I have this ring,

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.730
the whole world is like 
a bonus stage for me.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.460
Now, let's start the game!

00:03:57.150 --> 00:04:00.400
What game are you starting, sir?

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:05.380
The overpowering aura of a Horologue 
is pouring out of that ring.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.860
Who are you?

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.750
You guys are from Chronos, huh?

00:04:11.090 --> 00:04:12.480
Sounds fun.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:16.230
The more players in a game,
the more fun it is!

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.230
Go! We'll start by conquering these guys!

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:22.520
Do you think it'll be that easy?

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.080
Slow Down.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.490
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.490
Slow Down.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:32.750
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:54.270
There's no way he could survive 
a fall from this height.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:57.770
Hey! Warn me before you do that! 
You scared the piss outta me!

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:58.790
You idiot!

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:02.800
If we'd waited, everyone on board would've 
been eaten, and then it'd be game over!

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:09.030
You surprised me. That was a nice combo.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.540
I bet you'd be good at fighting games.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:16.540
First you used Slow Down 
to create a wall of air,

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:19.790
isolating the area around
the door from the other passengers.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:24.010
Then you opened the emergency exit
and launched us all out.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.390
I haven't introduced myself, have I?

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:30.530
My name is Bill Reidan.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.840
I'm a gamer.

00:05:32.570 --> 00:05:33.790
And...

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:41.800
This is the servant I've summoned,

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:42.860
Bahamut!

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:49.620
An animal-type Horologue.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.100
Well, what style should we play?

00:05:53.100 --> 00:05:54.240
Style?

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:56.840
One-on-one fighting game style,

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.130
or one-on-many RPG style?

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.160
Ah, I get it.

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.250
Sorry, though.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.380
If you want to play video games,
play them at home.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:11.290
At the very least,
this is not the place for them.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.690
Big words.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.030
Ready...

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:17.250
Fight!

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:30.530
Given its size, that must be at least 
a thousand-year-class Horologue.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.900
Maybe it's time to test 
this gift from Snake.

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:36.940
What're you going to do with a cell phone?

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.220
This is the problem with you old men.

00:06:39.220 --> 00:06:43.170
There's an app installed on this 
that analyzes Horologues' data.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:46.010
<i>Hi there! My name's Miko!</i>

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.420
<i>I'm a high school girl here to
help you battle Horologues!</i>

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:50.840
<i>I hope we'll be great friends, Kiri!</i>

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:55.790
<i>Before using the app, register your 
user account by looking at me</i>

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.850
<i>and shouting, "I love high 
school girls' panties!"</i>

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:04.000
I love high school girls' pan—

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.630
Like hell I can say that!

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.860
Damn you, Snake!

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:14.580
This is the problem with you virgins.

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.180
I'll show you how it's done.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:23.380
I love high school girls' panties!

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:26.100
<i>Eek! Kiri, you're so dirty!</i>

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.440
<i>But that's just the way I like you!</i>

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:34.730
Bastard!

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:49.690
<i>Now to start taking measurements.</i>

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.920
<i>Line up the cursor with the Horologue.</i>

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.200
<i>Why is this the cursor?</i>

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.200
<i>Whatever. Have it your way.</i>

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.580
<b>Measurement Complete</b>

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:58.510
<i>Measurement complete.</i>

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:02.230
<i>The target Horologue is 
a form-2 animal type.</i>

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:03.960
<i>The time it has consumed is...</i>

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:07.330
Wha...

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:11.700
I-It's a 3,800-year-class?!

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:13.720
Hey, come on...

00:08:13.980 --> 00:08:16.720
Is it even fun to play by pecking 
at a little thing like that?

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:21.730
There's no game more exhilarating 
than the reality we're in right now!

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:29.070
Oh? You're a water elemental, eh?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:32.570
I see. The quiet, composed character, 
just as your looks would imply.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:34.870
You've got your backstory down pat.

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:36.820
Don't you lay a hand...

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:42.040
on my little brother!

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:38.780
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:45.190
A fire elemental, huh?

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:47.290
That explains the hot temper.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:48.530
Shut up!

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:50.710
Instant Destruction by Fire!

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.050
But you know, fire and water elementals...

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.930
cancel each other out!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.690
Damn it! I'll teach you to mock me!

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.390
Sounds like you're very perceptive.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.460
What do you think I am, then?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.640
Wind elemental.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:19.200
The free-spirited wannabe princess 
who hates to be restrained, right?

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:20.120
Bingo!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:29.210
Leave it to a 3,800-year class to have 
this kind of defensive strength.

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:32.440
But at a time like this, 
if this were a game...

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.970
There's something to be said for 
targeting the summoner instead.

00:09:46.690 --> 00:09:48.400
Game over.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.400
What's going on? Do you not feel pain?

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:00.640
Pain? What are you talking about?

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.910
This is a game, you know.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.410
Why would it hurt?

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:10.110
Oh, but my HP is already down 50%...

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.730
Well done!

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:16.700
<i>He can't even tell reality 
from a video game anymore.</i>

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.680
<i>Why take this so far?</i>

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:23.180
Hey, you just thought,
"Why take this so far?" Didn't you?

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:27.430
I'll tell you. For me, the real world...

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:30.690
has turned into a game!

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:37.020
There's nothing really special about me.

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.200
I have no friends in reality.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:44.820
Being in the reality they call 
"school" was genuinely painful.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:21.870
It was video games that 
saved me from all that.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:25.790
I only truly enjoyed myself 
when playing video games,

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:29.390
and I even found some people online 
that I could almost call "friends."

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:35.340
I thought I'd never have to return 
to the reality of "school" again.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:55.740
After that, I continued 
living as an invalid would,

00:11:55.740 --> 00:11:59.190
and my only living relative, 
my mother, said nothing.

00:11:59.190 --> 00:12:02.250
She just did everything I told 
her to, like a good servant.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:05.650
But then, one day,

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:09.200
it was suddenly game over.

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:11.720
She worked herself to death,

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:15.580
doing both the housework and 
the breadwinning all alone.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.800
I regretted everything.

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.170
I begged time to turn back.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:30.140
And then a man said this to me...

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:33.270
<i>It's not game over yet.</i>

00:12:33.270 --> 00:12:37.020
<i>If you collect time from other 
people and reverse its flow,</i>

00:12:37.020 --> 00:12:39.260
<i>you can get your mother back.</i>

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:50.290
Yes... So long as I have this ring,

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:56.380
I can rewrite the "reality" 
of my past into a game!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:00.460
That's why, for me, reality is

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:05.300
a game!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.460
Everything is a game!

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.940
I don't have to feel pain,

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:20.250
and I don't have to worry about anything!

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:24.110
So come on! How are you 
going to play with me?

00:13:40.480 --> 00:13:43.960
Hey! Where are you going?! 
Don't go that way!

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:06.740
First of all, we'll need you to 
shut down that crappy console.

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:15.110
The real world is not a game.

00:14:23.330 --> 00:14:25.590
Oh, no! It's out of control!

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:28.220
Slow Down!

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.800
I'll start by hardening my cards!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.800
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:30.800
Victor!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.030
Show me UNIQUE's true strength!

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.470
<b>Slow Down</b>

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:36.480
Speed Up!

00:14:47.860 --> 00:14:50.120
<i>A single strike?</i>

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:55.790
<i>So this is the power of UNIQUE, 
the original Oath of Time?</i>

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:01.710
Really? Is this the time to be zoning out?

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:12.330
<i>My Bahamut...</i>

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.570
Is everyone all right?

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.760
Yeah... Sort of...

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.690
Mom... Mom...

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.790
Did you really die?

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:55.620
To be honest, I knew it was all real.

00:15:56.670 --> 00:16:00.350
This world isn't a game at all.

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:28.600
Bill, your mother may be 
gone from this world,

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:33.000
but you haven't lost your memories of 
the time you spent with her, right?

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:42.360
That means your mother can live 
forever inside your heart.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.750
I... I...

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.280
I shut myself in my room every day,

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:56.080
just playing video games.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:00.320
I treated my mom like some kind of slave.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.690
And I said all kinds of awful things to her.

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:27.750
And yet, right up to the 
day she left this world,

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:34.030
I never said, "Thank you," to her even once!

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:30.480
I'm sorry

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.600
You're right.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.040
I haven't lost my memories of my mom.

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:46.360
That's why... That's exactly why...

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:51.420
It's so painful!

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:56.650
I haven't forgotten, because I <i>can't</i> forget!

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:59.050
What am I supposed to do?!

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.930
Tell me!

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.620
Is this what you want, Victor?

00:19:47.630 --> 00:19:50.300
We could get information 
on Horologues from him.

00:19:51.030 --> 00:19:52.790
No, it doesn't matter.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:55.900
He's the lowest form of humanity, anyway.

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:07.600
You look pale. Are you all right?

00:20:09.300 --> 00:20:10.960
I'm totally fine!

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.850
I could eat pasta through my nose right now!

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:23.570
Wow... So he lost his mom, too.

00:20:23.970 --> 00:20:26.750
That's gotta hurt so much.

00:20:31.130 --> 00:20:33.380
This is getting on my nerves.

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.210
Stop crying!

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:37.150
Let's go, Blaze.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:39.460
Sh-Shut up! I'm not crying!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.510
I told you, it's just sweat!

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.290
You liar! I know you were crying!

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:45.670
I was not!

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:47.930
You totally, totally were!

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:49.520
<i>How much easier it would be</i>

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:54.100
<i>if I could follow my emotions 
and express how I really feel,</i>

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:55.520
<i>just like they do...</i>

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:59.570
<i>But I can't do that.</i>

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:06.700
Well, let's go.

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:09.710
Couljours shouldn't be too far from here.

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:18.130
<i>You only try to act like 
a father at times like this,</i>

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:22.050
<i>playing tough and taking 
everything on alone.</i>

00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.820
<i>That's obvious to anyone,</i>

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:27.980
<i>Victor.</i>

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:51.450
The Poverty of Philosophy

00:21:51.450 --> 00:21:54.660
The Poverty of Philosophy

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:54.700
The Poverty of Philosophy

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:54.790
The Poverty of Philosophy

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:54.870
The Poverty of Philosophy

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:40.100
Fact and Fiction
